# linkedin's risk disclosure for sending (core/modules/linkedin/README.md "API"): before an account
# sends anything, its owner accepts the current version and confirms it is their own personal
# account. One variable besides the usual ones goes in http-client.private.env.json: `accountId`, an
# id GET …/linkedin/accounts answers. The route is @Idempotent(): the Idempotency-Key is an example
# UUID; another one presses again, the same one answers the first answer again for a day. A write
# sends the cookie, so it sends Origin: {{appOrigin}} too.

### POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/linkedin/accounts/{id}/disclosure: the owner accepts the disclosure for sending; 200 with the account, sendingDisclosureRequired false; 400 disclosure_version_invalid or personal_account_required; 403 not_account_owner
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/linkedin/accounts/{{accountId}}/disclosure
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
Origin: {{appOrigin}}
Idempotency-Key: 00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000001070

{ "version": 2, "personalAccount": true }
